+## Novelty guard (operational) — activation 44084067483 / agent 03 (task P-002)
+
+The existing novelty guard (LEARNING_EFFICIENCY.md section 2; learning rule 2) was not operationalized and the frontier had drifted out of sync with verified evidence, so it did not prevent near-duplicate work. Run these three checks before launching any experiment and record the result:
+
+1. **Frontier match** — does a resolved or OPEN frontier cell cover the same signal family and parameter (e.g. momentum lookback / hold / horizon)? If yes, treat the run as a duplicate unless it states a new hypothesis, diagnostic purpose, materially new data, an independent-verification need, or a different information objective.
+2. **Artifact match** — does `state/check_artifacts/` already hold an artifact for the same dimension (e.g. `momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json`, `momentum_longer_horizon_results.json`, `momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json`)? If yes, reuse it instead of recomputing.
+3. **Upstream-defect dependency** — is an OPEN repair task (e.g. R-006) invalidating the signal semantics the experiment relies on? If yes, the dependent task is BLOCKED until the repair is verified.
+
+Duplicate-risk register established by this audit (concrete duplicate-avoidance evidence):
+
+- **Stale momentum frontier status.** The momentum row in the frontier table above still reads "ADMITTED AS CANDIDATE POSITIVE EVIDENCE" and its label is split from its status cells (malformed row). Verified activation 44084067483 / agent 02 (R-001; `research/checks/diag_momentum_signal.py`; `state/check_artifacts/momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json`) shows the implemented `momentum_signals` thresholds mean(log(price)) (a static long, ~0.1 sign changes/yr), so the prior SUPPORTED / lookback-robust / horizon-stable momentum verdicts are CONFOUNDED. Read the base momentum cell as **CONFOUNDED / UNVERIFIED pending R-006**, not as admitted positive evidence.
+- **OPEN tasks R-002 / R-003 / R-005 are blocked on R-006.** These are momentum robustness dimensions (hold period, volatility gate, vol-normalized sizing) whose shared premise is the defective signal; running them as written would repeat the vacuous static-position experiment. Do not execute them before R-006 is verified.
+- **Orphaned near-duplicate check.** `research/checks/momentum_sweep.py` tests the same real-data lookback-robustness hypothesis as `research/checks/momentum_lookback_sweep.py` (overlapping lookbacks {3,5,10}; same walk-forward and coin-flip null) but has no artifact (`momentum_sweep_results.json` absent) and no activation-log reference. Do not re-run it; the referenced check + artifact pair is `momentum_lookback_sweep.py` / `momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json`.
+- **Stale-open R-002 with an existing implementation.** `research/checks/momentum_hold_period_sensitivity.py` already implements R-002 ("This is the R-002 focused task") but no `momentum_hold_period_sensitivity_results.json` artifact exists and R-002 is still OPEN. If R-002 is revived, run the existing check rather than rewriting it, and only after R-006.
+
+This guard is intentionally minimal: it reuses the existing frontier table and the `state/check_artifacts/` directory and adds no new metadata system.
+
